{"type":"step-attempt","step":"conformance","sessionId":"4ff39175-2cf1-402f-87ec-0562c2a676d4","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/skeleton-and-parser/conformance-result-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":true,"findings":[{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/parse/references.ts","title":"Code fence detection uses trimStart() instead of startsWith()","rationale":"Both references.ts and declarations.ts use `line.trimStart().startsWith('```')` to detect code fences, whereas tools/check.sh anchors at `^`. Indented triple-backtick lines would incorrectly toggle fence state. No impact on current design/ documents (which use unindented fences), but diverges from check.sh algorithm.","line":61,"fixTarget":"code-fixer"},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/parse/declarations.ts","title":"findFrontmatterIdLine() scans the full file instead of the frontmatter block","rationale":"The helper scans all lines for `/^id:\\s/`, so a body line like `id: something` in a file without frontmatter could return a wrong line number. Only affects diagnostic position accuracy (falls back to 1). Functional behavior is correct.","fixTarget":"code-fixer"},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/parse/parser.ts","title":"Frontmatter is parsed twice per file (double-parse + deduplication workaround)","rationale":"parser.ts calls parseFrontmatter() directly (L34) and then extractDeclarations() (L39) which calls parseFrontmatter() internally again. The deduplication block at L44-51 is a workaround for the resulting duplicate diagnostics. A cleaner design would pass the pre-parsed FrontmatterResult into extractDeclarations().","line":34,"fixTarget":"code-fixer"},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/parse/parser.ts","title":"responsibilities, implementations, actorIds, elementItems not propagated to ParseResult","rationale":"extractStructuredLines() returns these fields but parser.ts only uses dependencyEdges. spec.md states the parser SHALL recognize structured lines 'within the parse result', but ParseResult (D4) has no fields for them. No consumer exists yet; next request can extend ParseResult when needed.","fixTarget":"code-fixer"}]},"followUpAttempts":1,"transientRetryAttempts":0},"startedAt":"2026-07-02T03:06:44.407Z","endedAt":"2026-07-02T03:12:20.715Z"}
